{
  "note": "Committed REACH floors for the repo's scanning guards, one row per scan. Floors only go UP. `reach < floor` is a REGRESSION: the scan shrank, so every verdict derived from it is worthless until that is explained. A scan with no row FAILS rather than defaulting — a closed universe is the only thing that stops a new guard shipping with no reach at all. Lock in growth with `bun run scan-reach --tighten`, which refuses while any scan is below its floor and rewrites only rows that already exist. `walked` proves the anchor (the scan reached a real corpus); `matched` proves the predicate (the guard's own matcher still selects something) — a matcher that rotted selects nothing while the walk stays full.",
